en.value:
&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;u&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Article - 249&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/u&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Article 249 of the Indian constitution is related to the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Legislative Powers of parliament&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;with respect to subjects in the state list. It empowers the Parliament to make laws with respect to any matter enumerated in the state list.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;The President can declare three types of emergencies:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;National Emergency-&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;Article 352&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;State Emergency-&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;Article 356&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Financial Emergency-&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;Article 360&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Dissolution of the Lok Sabha&amp;ndash;Article 83(2)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Article 253:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;confers&lt;/strong&gt; powers on the Parliament to make laws to implement international agreements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Article 223&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;deals with the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;appointment of acting Chief Justice&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;when the office of Chief Justice of High Court is vacant.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Article 293- States about the Borrowing by the state.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

