&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Prathna Sabha -&lt;/span&gt;​&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It is a community &lt;strong&gt;established&lt;/strong&gt; for &lt;strong&gt;religious&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;social reforms &lt;/strong&gt;during the &lt;strong&gt;Indian Renaissance.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It was founded by&lt;strong&gt; Atmaram Pandurang,&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Mahadev Govind Ranade&lt;/strong&gt;, and&lt;strong&gt; R.G. Bhandarkar on 31 March 1867&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;Bombay.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/additional-information-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Additional Information&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Atmiya Sabha&amp;nbsp;-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Its&lt;strong&gt; founder was Raja Ram Mohan Roy.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It was &lt;strong&gt;established in Calcutta&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;1815&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It was a platform for the discussion of independent philosophical ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;This assembly supported independent thought and &lt;strong&gt;social reforms.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;This gathering itself was named&lt;strong&gt; &amp;#39;Brahma Samaj&amp;#39; in 1828.&lt;/strong&gt;​&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Home Rule League -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It was a &lt;strong&gt;national political organization&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It was &lt;strong&gt;founded in 1916 &lt;/strong&gt;by &lt;strong&gt;Bal Gangadhar Tilak&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the &lt;strong&gt;national demand for self-government &lt;/strong&gt;in India.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;This was done to get India the status of a Dominion in the British Raj.​&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Ramakrishna&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Mission -&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;It was &lt;strong&gt;founded on May 1, 1897&lt;/strong&gt;, by &lt;strong&gt;Swami Vivekananda&lt;/strong&gt;, the supreme disciple of Ramakrishna Paramhansa.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Its&lt;strong&gt; headquarter is at Belur &lt;/strong&gt;near Kolkata.&lt;br /&gt;
		Propagation of &lt;strong&gt;Vedanta philosophy &lt;/strong&gt;is central to the establishment of this mission.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

