&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Indian Mutiny of 1857&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;was a major revolt in India against the rule of the British East India Company, which acted as a sovereign power on behalf of the British Crown.

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The rebellion began on&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;10 May 1857&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;as a mutiny by soldiers of the Company&amp;#39;s army in the garrison town of Meerut.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The rebellion posed a great threat to British power in that region and was only contained with the defeat of the rebels at Gwalior on&lt;strong&gt; 20 June 1858&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Its name has been contested and has been described as the&amp;nbsp;Sepoy Mutiny, the Indian Rebellion, the Great Rebellion, the Rebellion of 1857, the Indian Rebellion, and the First War of Independence.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

