	&lt;/tbody&gt;
&lt;/table&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;जब कोई&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;एक शब्द&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;किसी दूसरे शब्द का&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;उल्टा&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;या&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;विपरीत&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;अर्थ व्यक्त करे तो उसे&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;विलोम शब्द&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;कहा जाता है।&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/important-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Important Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;कुछ महत्वपूर्ण विलोम शब्द:-&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;शब्द -&amp;nbsp;विलोम&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;तामसिक -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space:pre&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;सात्विक&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;नैसर्गिक -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;कृत्रिम&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;सविकार -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;निर्विकार&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;नास्तिक -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;आस्तिक&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;वैमनस्य&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; - &lt;/span&gt;सौमनस्य&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;सकाम -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;निष्काम&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;अनुरक्ति -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre;&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;विरक्ति&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;ज्योतिर्मय -&lt;span style=&quot;white-space:pre&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;तमोमय&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;अरण्य का पर्यायवाची शब्द है :&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;कानन&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;कानन :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;कानन&amp;#39; के अन्य पर्यायवाची &amp;#39;अरण्य, जंगल, कान्तार, विपिन&amp;#39; हैं।&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;वाटिका, बाग़, उपवन:- ये सभी बगीचा बाग़ के पर्यायवाची है।&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;अरण्य अर्थात वन प्राकृतिक होते हैं और बगीचा या बाग़ मानव निर्मित होता है।&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/important-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Important Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;कपोत- कबूतर, हारीत, पारावत, परेवा, रक्तलोचन।&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;कपूर- घनसार,हिमवालुका।&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;गाय- भद्रा, गौरी, सुरभी, धेनु, गऊ, गौ,गैया, पयसि्वनी,दोग्धी&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;छाछ- गोरस, मठा, दधि स्वेद, मट्ठा।&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;द्रौपदी- कृष्णा, पांचाली, सैरंध्री, याज्ञसेनी।&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;मोक्ष- कैवल्य, मुक्ति, सद्गति, निर्वाण, परम पद।&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;was restricted&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Lets analyze the following sentence from the given passage -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Unlike in the olden days, its performance is no longer restricted to villages or small localities of the city.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The sentence establishes the concept that in the olden days, performance of street theatre only happened in the villages or small localities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The best phrase to describe this is &amp;#39;was restricted&amp;#39; which implies that something is&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;available only to particular groups.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Hence,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 2&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct word for the given blank.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Complete sentence&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;In the olden days, street theatre &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;was restricted&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to villages or small localities of the city.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;reform&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stabilization&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is a noun which means&amp;nbsp;the process of becoming or being made unlikely to change, fail, or decline.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let us look into the meaning of the given options -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ancient -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;belonging to the very distant past and no longer in existence.(&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;1st&amp;nbsp;line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Street theatre in India is a well established &lt;u&gt;ancient &lt;/u&gt;art form.&amp;#39;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;propagating -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;spread and promote (an idea, theory, etc.) widely. (&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;3rd line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;... has for centuries been &lt;u&gt;propagating &lt;/u&gt;reforms by highlighting social, economic and political issues present in the society.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;#39;)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;established -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;having existed or done something for a long time and therefore recognized and generally accepted.(&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;1st&amp;nbsp;line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Street theatre in India is a well &lt;u&gt;established&amp;nbsp;&lt;/u&gt;ancient&amp;nbsp;art form.&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;reform -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;make changes in (something, especially an institution or practice) in order to improve it.(&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;3rd line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;... has for centuries been propagating &lt;u&gt;reforms &lt;/u&gt;by highlighting social, economic and political issues present in the society.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;From the above meanings it is clear that&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;reform&amp;#39;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the&amp;nbsp;word&amp;nbsp;with the meaning opposite to &amp;lsquo;&lt;strong&gt;stabilization&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;lsquo; in the passage.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 4&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;despite&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regardless &lt;/strong&gt;means&amp;nbsp;despite the prevailing circumstances;&amp;nbsp;without regard or consideration for.

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;Example - The allowance is paid &lt;strong&gt;regardless &lt;/strong&gt;of age or income.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let us look into the meaning of the given options -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;mobilize -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;organize and encourage (a group of people) to take collective action in pursuit of a particular objective.&amp;nbsp;(&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;5th line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;... would stage performances to mobilize public opinion ...&amp;#39;)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;restricted -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;limited in extent, number, scope, or action. (&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;4th line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;... its performance is no longer restricted to ...&amp;#39;)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;contemporary -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;living or occurring at the same time. (&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;6th line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;... are some of the areas highlighted by contemporary street theatre troupe.&amp;nbsp;&amp;#39;)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;despite -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;without being affected by the particular factor mentioned. (&lt;em&gt;used in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;2nd line&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given passage - &amp;#39;&lt;/em&gt;Despite the proliferation of modern means ...&amp;#39;)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;From the above meanings it is clear that&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;despite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the&amp;nbsp;word in the passage means &amp;#39;&lt;strong&gt;regardless&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 4&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct answer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is &amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; &quot;&gt;I was asked my name by the interviewer.&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;active voice.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;As per the question we have to change it into&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;passive voice.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The structure of the given sentence is as follows:
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subject + past participle + Object (Active voice)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Subject (objective case) + was + past participle + by Object (subjective case) (Passive voice)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Example:&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;She built a large garden. (Active voice)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;A large garden was built by her. (Passive voice)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;subject&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given sentence is &amp;lsquo;the interviewer&amp;rsquo;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;object&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;of the given sentence is &amp;lsquo;me&amp;rsquo;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The subject will be put in place of the object and the object will be put in place of the subject.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;asked&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;will be changed to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;was asked&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Me&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is changed to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;I&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;in the passive voice.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Correct sentence -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;I was asked my name by the interviewer.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 4&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct answer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;No article&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;In English there are three articles:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;a&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;an&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;, and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;the&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;Articles are used before nouns or noun equivalents and are a type of adjective. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;definite article (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;the&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(68, 68, 68);   &quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;)&lt;/strong&gt; is used before a noun to indicate that the identity of the noun is known to the reader. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The indefinite article (a,&amp;nbsp;an) is used before a noun that is general or when its identity is not known.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;There are certain situations in which a noun takes no article.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We use no article with plural count nouns or any noncount nouns used to mean all or in general.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Noncount nouns&lt;/strong&gt; are those which usually cannot be counted.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Sugar&amp;nbsp;is an uncountable noun.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Hence, we do not need to add any article before it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 2&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;or&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;No article&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is the correct answer.&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Complete sentence&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sugar is good for our health.&lt;/em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The correct answer is&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;Tranquil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let us see the&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;meanings&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the given options:

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tranquil:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;quiet and peaceful. (शांत, प्रशांत)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Agitated:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;worried or excited. (परेशान या उत्तेजित)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chaotic:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;in a state of chaos. (अव्&amp;zwj;यवस्थित, अस्&amp;zwj;त व्&amp;zwj;यस्&amp;zwj;त)&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Violent:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;using physical strength to hurt or kill somebody; caused by this behaviour. (जिसमें किसी को चोट पहुँचाने या मारने के लिए भौतिक शक्ति का प्रयोग हो, हिंसक; हिंसात्&amp;zwj;मक, हिंसापूर्ण)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;From the&amp;nbsp;meanings of the given words, we can say that&amp;nbsp;one word substitute for&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;Free from disturbance&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt; is &lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;Tranquil.&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Hence, the correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Option 1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The correct answer is&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;spent lavishly&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul style=&quot;&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The meaning of the idiom&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;played ducks and drakes&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;is&amp;nbsp;to carelessly misuse, spent one&amp;rsquo;s wealth.&amp;nbsp;(Idiom&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Played ducks and drakes&amp;quot;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;का अर्थ किसी के धन का लापरवाही से दुरुपयोग करना।)

	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;Example:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;Jane &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;played duck and drakes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt; with the financial system of company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lavishly &lt;/strong&gt;means&amp;nbsp;in a sumptuously rich, elaborate, or luxurious manner;&amp;nbsp;in a very generous or extravagant manner; in profusion.&amp;nbsp;(बहुत उदार या असाधारण तरीके से; बहुतायत में;&amp;nbsp;एक समृद्ध रूप से, विस्तृत या शानदार तरीके से)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So, the most appropriate meaning of the given idiom&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;is&lt;strong&gt; &amp;quot;spent lavishly.&amp;quot;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;​​&lt;/em&gt;Therefore, the correct option is&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Option 4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(i) - d, (ii) - c, (iii) - b, (iv) - a&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;#39;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Lets look into the usage of the given prepositions -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(a) on&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;- used to having (the thing mentioned) as a target, aim, or focus. -&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;This dress is now available &lt;strong&gt;on &lt;/strong&gt;sale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;(b) with -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;used to indicate&amp;nbsp;responsibility - &lt;i&gt;He left it &lt;strong&gt;with &lt;/strong&gt;me.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;(c) for -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; line-height: 107%; &quot;&gt;used to&amp;nbsp;talk about a purpose or a reason for something. -&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m going&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;some breakfast.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;(d) to -&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; line-height: 107%; &quot;&gt;identifying the person or thing affected by or receiving something.&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;i&gt;You sent the letter&amp;nbsp;&lt;b&gt;to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;her.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;From the above usage descriptions we can conclude that -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The preposition&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;(a) on&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;is appropriate for&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;sentence (iv)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;-&amp;nbsp;This car is &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;on&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;sale, if you are keen to buy it.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The preposition&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;(b) with&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;is appropriate for&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;sentence (iii)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;-&amp;nbsp;I am not satisfied &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;your-explanation.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The preposition&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;(c) for&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;is appropriate for&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;sentence (ii)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;-&amp;nbsp;I have got a meeting &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Thursday afternoon.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The preposition&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;(d) to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;is appropriate for&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;sentence (i)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;-&amp;nbsp;She is grateful &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;to&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;her friend for her help.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Thus, the matches that we get are -&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 700; &quot;&gt;(i) - d, (ii) - c, (iii) - b, (iv) - a&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Hence,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 1&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;has been sleeping&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Let us look at the verb/tense forms of the given options -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;is sleeping -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;present continuous tense&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;was sleeping -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;past continuous tense&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;has been sleeping -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;present perfect continuous tense&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;slept -&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;simple past tense&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;From the given sentence it is evident that the child started sleeping in the past and that action is continuing.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;We use the &lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Present Perfect Continuous tense &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;to talk about action that started in the past and is continuing now.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;So, the correct tense form in the given blank is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;has been sleeping.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Thus,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 3&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct answer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br /&gt;
	&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Complete sentence&lt;/u&gt;&amp;nbsp;-&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;quot;The child&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;has been sleeping&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/u&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;for the last one hour.&amp;quot;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The correct answer is&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;#39;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;John said that he had waited for Lisa till 10 O&amp;#39;clock.&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;display: flex;gap: 6px;align-items: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;img height=&quot;26px&quot; src=&quot;//cdn.testbook.com/resources/lms_creative_elements/key-point-image.png&quot; width=&quot;26px&quot; /&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;vertical-align: middle;font-size: 21px;&quot;&gt;&lt;u&gt;Key Points&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;The given sentence is an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;assertive sentence.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;While&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;changing the narration of an assertive sentence,&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;we need to follow steps -&amp;nbsp;
	&lt;ul&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;reporting verb said&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;remains unchanged.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;conjunction &amp;#39;that&amp;#39;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;is used in place of commas and inverted commas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;pronoun I&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is in&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;first person&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;and should be changed to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;third person he.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;simple past tense verb &amp;#39;waited&amp;#39;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is changed to&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;past perfect tense &amp;#39;had waited&amp;#39;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ul&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Eventually, we will get the final sentence- &lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;John said that he had waited for Lisa till 10 O&amp;#39;clock.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;&quot;&gt;So,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;option 4&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is the correct answer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
